   <h3> Guild Roles</h3>
   <p>
   
<p><b>Raid Commander</b></p>
<p>The sole responsibility of the Raid Commander is to arrange and organize a 
  guild-wide raid. This can be anything from a basic raid of Cazic Thule to a 
  Planes raid. The Raid Commander should discuss the raid planning with an officer 
  of the Circle of Bones and set the goals for the raid (are we going after a 
  specific critter? Are we &quot;doing&quot; a dungeon? Are we there to learn 
  the zone? etc.). Once the raid place, date, time, and goals have been established 
  and approved by the Circle of Bones, the raid will be announced on the guild 
  website at least 5 days in advance and announced on guild chat.</p>
<p>The Raid Commander is expected to be at the raids planned. If the Raid Commander 
  cannot be there for some reason (real life obligations, etc.). The Raid Commander 
  must appoint a temporary &quot;Raid Master&quot; who will be in charge of conducting 
  the raid and must be present at the raid</p>
<p><b>Recruiters</b></p>
<p>The recruiting position is an important role within the guild. They are the 
  main contact between the guild and new potential members. All inquiries about 
  guild membership should be directed to one of the guild recruiters. The responsibilities 
  of a recruiter includes:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Be the initial contact with new potential members and a public relations 
    to help recruit new members.</li>
  <li>Make sure that potential member fit within the Bloodhorde guidelines.</li>
  <li>Get a good feeling for potential new members and filter out the &quot;not 
    so good&quot; ones.</li>
  <li>Send a weekly email report to the Circle of Bones listing any new recruits.</li>
</ol>
<p><b>Guild Meeting Coordinator</b></p>
<p>Responsible for organizing one guild-wide meeting (in guild chat) and one Circle 
  of Bones meeting a month.</p>
<p><b>Guild Recruit Initiator</b></p>
<p>Reponsible for properly initiating all new members by setting up duels for 
  them and providing an initiation ceremony.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><b>Battalion Dragoon and Crusader</b></p>
<p>The Battalion Dragoon and Crusader are to be considered co-leaders of a battalion. 
  The Dragoon and Crusader are to be the same level range as their battalion and 
  are expected to hunt with their battalion. The Dragoon and Crusader are responsible 
  for choosing the hunting spot for their Battalion. The hunting spot should have 
  a priority of good experience for members of the Battalion, with possible item 
  drops as a distant secondary concern, unless otherwise directed by their commanding 
  Blood Knight. The Battalion is strongly encouraged to stay at a chosen hunting 
  spot for at least one week. This allows members of the battalion to get there, 
  get bound near by, and have a consistent place to hunt with guild members without 
  the need to run around the world each time they log on. </p>
<p>The Dragoon and Crusader are given different roles and responsibilities for 
  clarity. However, either one should should be able to handle all responsibilities 
  if the other is not present.</p>
<p>Since the Dragoon and Crusader are required to hunt with their battalion. There 
  will come a time when they have advanced in level beyond their own battalion. 
  At this point the Dragoon and Crusader should consult with each other and pick 
  a member from their battalion that is worthy of taking over the position. Once 
  they have chosen a person to fill the vacant position, they should discuss it 
  with their commanding Bone Guard or Blood Knight. If it is approved, the chosen 
  member will be moved to the Dragoon or Crusader position.</p>
<p><b>NOTE</b>: It should be made clear that if a member is a Dragoon or Crusader 
  of a lower level Battalion, it does not guarantee that they will hold that position 
  in a higher level battalion. Do not expect to be promoted to Dragoon/Crusader 
  again just because you were a Dragoon/Crusader before. When you move up, there 
  are many people in front of you for that position.</p>
<p><b>Battalion Dragoon</b></p>
<p>Overall, the Dragoon is responsible for the management of the Battalion. The 
  Dragoon responsibilities include:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Be the leader and morale boost for their Battalion</li>
  <li>handle all Battalion issues (member conflicts, arguments, etc.). If the 
    Dragoon is unable to resolve an issue, he/she should contact their commanding 
    Bone Guard. </li>
  <li>Posting the current hunting spot on the Battalion's page on the website.</li>
  <li>Loot distribution - the Dragoon is responsible for making sure their Battalion 
    understands how items are distributed and enforcing/encouraging that distribution 
    method. It is strongly suggested that the guild <a href="/index.pl?node=Loot%20Distribution&lastnode_id=1059">Loot Distribution</a> rules 
    and guidelines are followed.
  <li>Finding new hunting spots</li>
</ol>
<p><b>Battalion Crusader</b></p>
<p>The Crusader focuses on the hunt and battle. The Crusader responsibilities 
  include:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Be the leader and morale boost for their Battalion</li>
  <li>Strongly encourage members to hunt at the chosen hunting spot.</li>
  <li>Actively work to make sure their battalion members are grouped with each 
    other as much as possible. This also includes telling who to group with who 
    and rearranging groups as necessary to make the hunt as productive and fun 
    as possible.</li>
  <li>Help members work on battle strategies</li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>

